        "original_id": "8c122600-5f2a-5033-bb99-5d5d7f6413cf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Wesley, Charles Wesley, George Whitefield, Edward Perronet\n- Organizations: Church of England, Methodism\n- Roles: Anglican cleric, theologian, Anglican priest\n- Events: 18th-century revival\n\nFacts:\n- Methodism originated as a revival within the 18th-century Church of England.\n- John Wesley was born on 28 June 1703 O.S. 17 June 1703.\n- John Wesley was an English Anglican cleric and theologian.\n- John Wesley, Charles Wesley, and George Whitefield founded Methodism.\n- Edward Perronet was born in 1726 and was the son of an Anglican priest.\n- Edward Perronet worked closely with Anglican priest John Wesley and Charles Wesley for many years during England's eighteenth-century revival.\n- John Wesley died on 2 March 1791.\n- Methodism became a separate denomination after John Wesley's death.\n- Edward Perronet died on 2 January 1792.",
